From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] print status: stats and IFS card instead of the printer picture

The Print Status screen's printer tile drops the printer picture, its
leader lines and glows. In its place, stat tiles two to a row: nozzle
and bed, part fan and speed/flow, the chamber when it reads (caption and
value; a tint and a bar on the left while a heater heats, the fan runs
or speed/flow is overridden; a tap opens the same overlays as the chips
did). Below them the IFS: a colour swatch per slot with its number,
material and what is left, the loaded slot ringed and an empty slot
dimmed, bound to AmsState's ams_slot_<n>_* subjects; during a swap,
load or unload a line above the swatches says what the IFS is doing
(ams_action_detail). The IFS part hides on a printer without one.
Stacked (portrait), the captions give their height up.

Sizes and flow are attributes on each object: a style's size loses to
the object's own default, and LVGL ignores a growing item's width when
it wraps a flex row (tried on the printer at 800x480).

With no ps_printer_area in the tree, PrintStatusTiles already publishes
the ps_chip_* subjects without a callout layout; there the fans now
publish without their label, as each stat has its own caption.
---
 src/ui/ui_print_status_tiles.cpp              |   6 +-
 .../components/print_status_printer_tile.xml  | 360 +++++++++++-------
 2 files changed, 237 insertions(+), 129 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ui/ui_print_status_tiles.cpp b/src/ui/ui_print_status_tiles.cpp
index 3052d45f83..3752753bd0 100644
--- a/src/ui/ui_print_status_tiles.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/ui_print_status_tiles.cpp
@@ -515,9 +515,13 @@ void PrintStatusTiles::update_now() {
 
     if (!area || !probe) {
         // No printer tile in this tree: the chips publish their content alone.
+        // Fans without their label: each stat in Kiln OS's tile has a caption.
         for (size_t i = 0; i < kPrintStatusChipCount; ++i) {
             const auto chip = static_cast<PrintStatusChip>(i);
-            publish(chip, contents[i], contents[i].shown, false, false);
+            const bool fan = chip == PrintStatusChip::PartFan ||
+                             chip == PrintStatusChip::HotendFan || chip == PrintStatusChip::AuxFan;
+            const ChipContent& c = fan ? bare[i] : contents[i];
+            publish(chip, c, c.shown, false, false);
         }
         return;
     }
